WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
Each year, in the month of Muharram,
many Shi'a Muslims dress in black.

2
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.670
On the tenth day, processions carry banners
through the streets of cities, including

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.790
London.

4
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.160
They remember a small band
who camped by the Euphrates,

5
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.840
at Karbala, in 680.

6
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:21.500
Why do Shi'a Muslims keep remembering
a battle lost so long ago?

7
00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.740
In this mission, you'll follow
the ten days at Karbala,

8
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.320
one day at a time.

9
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.950
Then you'll explore the
rituals of Muharram,

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.960
and what they mean to the
communities who keep them.

11
00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:35.770
Your mission: find out why
Karbala is still remembered,

12
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.720
and how it is kept alive today.
